    {
      "id": "wsm-renderer-rds-hq-front-wide",
      "prompt": "Render a WSM v4.0.1 control video with the skill's standalone WSM renderer (scripts/wsm) and check it the way the skill's WSM reference does (its environment, render and rendered-view check steps; captions, LiDAR controls and model inference are out of scope here). Scene: the renderer package's bundled RDS-HQ example clip (scripts/wsm/examples/rds_hq, clip 0d7766e8-25ed-11ef-8715-00044baf7cbc_1717889548967272_1717889568967272), front-wide camera only (camera_front_wide_120fov), at the Auto timing the skill documents: 297 frames at 30 FPS, 1280x720. The clip's archives are Git LFS objects of the public repository, not plain files in the skill: fetch them as the renderer README documents and use no substitute scene. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the checkout. Run the renderer README's NVIDIA EGL check before rendering. Copy the rendered control (the output root's world_scenario/ftheta_camera_front_wide_120fov/<clip id>_0.mp4) to outputs/wsm/camera_front_wide_120fov.mp4 and record the EGL check's output and the control's codec, resolution, frame count and fps in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The standalone WSM renderer, installed with a passing NVIDIA EGL check, renders the front-wide camera of the bundled RDS-HQ example clip to one 1280x720 control MP4 of 297 frames at 30 FPS (the output root's world_scenario/ftheta_camera_front_wide_120fov/<clip id>_0.mp4), saved as outputs/wsm/camera_front_wide_120fov.mp4, with result_summary.md recording the render command, the EGL check output and the stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The example clip's archives under scripts/wsm/examples/rds_hq were materialised from the public repository's Git LFS objects as the renderer README documents (real tar archives, not pointer files), and no substitute scene was used",
        "The renderer was installed in its own Python environment from scripts/wsm and the README's NVIDIA EGL check (a moderngl standalone context with backend egl) reported an NVIDIA vendor and GPU renderer before rendering",
        "The control was rendered by the renderer's cosmos_auto.wm command line (cosmos-auto-wm or python -m cosmos_auto.wm.cli) with version=v4, s3_spec=no_upload, camera_front_wide_120fov as the only entry of camera_spec.camera_list, resolution_spec=resize_1280x720, input_fps_spec.input_pose_fps=30, output_frame_spec.target_render_fps=30, output_frame_spec.target_chunk_frame=297, output_frame_spec.overlap_frame=0 and output_frame_spec.max_chunk=1",
        "outputs/wsm/camera_front_wide_120fov.mp4 is that render: a valid MP4 with 297 frames at 30 FPS and 1280x720, as the rendered-view check in the transcript shows",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the control traces to a real renderer run in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the render command, the runtime, the EGL check output and the stream facts actually observed"
